==================================================
HOME PAGE — CURRENT TARGET
==================================================

The Home page is the main player dashboard.

Its purpose is to show the player's current status and give them one obvious next action.

The Home page should contain:

- Player name
- XP / level progression
- Coins
- Streak
- Current league
- Robo Specter
- Continue Your Journey
- Tower progression preview
- Word of the Day
- Lucky Wheel
- Settings access

The page should feel like a polished game rather than a generic educational dashboard.

Do not overcrowd it.

==================================================
1. SETTINGS GEAR — FIX THE POSITION
==================================================

The Settings interface itself has already been improved and is acceptable for now.

Do NOT redesign the inside of the Settings interface again unless a functional problem is discovered.

The remaining problem is the Settings gear icon on the Home page.

It is currently positioned incorrectly.

Move the Settings gear to the proper upper-left corner of the Home-page header/container.

It should look like a normal game/application settings button.

It must remain correctly positioned on both desktop and mobile layouts.

Do not merely change its appearance.
Actually fix its layout/position.

==================================================
2. SETTINGS — KEEP THE CURRENT IMPROVEMENT
==================================================

Keep the improved Settings interface.

The player's learning stage/grade must NOT be changeable from Settings.

Remove/keep removed the option that allows the player to switch between learning stages/grades.

Keep the useful existing settings such as:

- Theme
- Language
- Logout
- Close

Do not add unnecessary settings.

==================================================
3. ROBO SPECTER — MOVE HIM UP
==================================================

Robo Specter is currently too low on the Home page.

Move Robo Specter ABOVE "Continue Your Journey."

The intended hierarchy should be approximately:

Player status

↓
Robo Specter

↓
Continue Your Journey

↓
Tower progression

↓
Word of the Day / Lucky Wheel

Robo Specter should feel like the player's guide/companion.

His content should remain concise and useful.

Do not make him dominate the page.

==================================================
4. CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY — FIX THE FUNCTIONALITY
==================================================

This is one of the most important fixes.

Currently the Home page displays something similar to:

"Continue your first lesson"

but clicking it does not actually navigate anywhere.

Fix the real navigation.

For a new player:

Continue Your Journey
→ the actual first available lesson / existing lesson-selection flow.

For a returning player:

Continue Your Journey
→ the player's actual current/next lesson.

Do NOT hardcode Lesson 1 for everyone.

Do NOT create a fake destination.

Do NOT simply change the text.

Trace the existing lesson system and connect the Home-page button to the real lesson flow.

After implementing this, actually verify that clicking/tapping the button produces a real navigation/state transition.

==================================================
5. TUTORIAL / FIRST-TIME ONBOARDING
==================================================

The current tutorial is only partially working.

Current behavior:

- A message appears telling the player to start the first lesson.
- Other parts of the interface are disabled/dimmed.
- The Continue Your Journey button is NOT actually highlighted.
- Clicking Continue Your Journey does NOT work while the tutorial is active.
- Clicking around randomly can eventually make the tutorial disappear.

That is not acceptable.

Turn this into a real guided interaction.

For a new player:

STEP 1:
Show a concise instruction telling the player what to do.

STEP 2:
Visually highlight the actual Continue Your Journey control.

The highlight must surround/point to the actual clickable control, not merely display a sentence somewhere else on the screen.

STEP 3:
Temporarily prevent unrelated interactions.

STEP 4:
Allow the player to click/tap the highlighted Continue Your Journey control.

STEP 5:
That click must trigger the real lesson navigation.

STEP 6:
The tutorial must progress/complete normally.

The player must NOT:

- click random areas to dismiss it
- click multiple unrelated times
- refresh the browser
- become trapped

It must work with:

- Desktop mouse
- Mobile touch

Do not create a fake tutorial that only displays text.

==================================================
6. WORD OF THE DAY — REMOVE THE WRONG LOCK
==================================================

Word of the Day is currently locked behind defeating the first/second boss.

That is incorrect for the Home-page daily feature.

A new player should not be shown a daily feature that they cannot access because they have not yet defeated bosses that they cannot currently reach.

Make Word of the Day accessible from the Home page without requiring those boss defeats.

Use the existing Word of the Day logic/data if it already exists.

Do not create duplicate systems.

Do not fabricate content.

Make sure the player can actually open/use the feature.

==================================================
7. LUCKY WHEEL — UNLOCK + ACTUALLY ANIMATE
==================================================

The Lucky Wheel is currently locked behind boss progression.

Remove that inappropriate lock.

The Lucky Wheel should be available as a Home-page daily feature.

Then make the interaction actually behave like a wheel.

When activated:

1. The wheel visibly spins.
2. It rotates for a noticeable amount of time.
3. It slows down.
4. It stops on a reward.
5. The selected reward is clearly revealed.
6. The reward is granted exactly once.
7. The player cannot trigger multiple spins simultaneously.

Do NOT:

- immediately display the reward
- use a static wheel and fake the result
- create a disconnected animation
- create a second reward system if one already exists

Connect the animation to the existing reward-selection logic.

